			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@simevidas/109616656924330801",
			"author": {
				"name": "Šime Vidas",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@simevidas",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/296/269/911/252/050/original/3be48f420d9991d3.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-01T23:57:25.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Does font-weight: 900 serve as a fallback? Some browsers might attempt to synthesize that weight.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109616863883393267",
			"parentId": "109616657007366442",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109616863883393267",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-02T00:50:03.691Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@simevidas\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>simevidas</span></a></span> do you see a fallback case in play? I have it listed in both my @font-face blocks and usage instances</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109617127784895054",
			"parentId": "109616863883393267",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@simevidas/109617127744009496",
			"author": {
				"name": "Šime Vidas",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@simevidas",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/296/269/911/252/050/original/3be48f420d9991d3.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-02T01:57:09.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I was confused because Hex Franklin Tight does not have a \"wght\" axis, so the number 900 seemed wrong. I guess, it would be simpler to just use font-weight: bold in both places. Or even simpler, to not set font-weight anywhere, but instead set font-synthesis: none to prevent the browser from messing with the font.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109625880141648056",
			"parentId": "109617127784895054",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109625880141648056",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-01-03T15:03:00.871Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@simevidas\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>simevidas</span></a></span> if you don’t set it, it’s implied to 400 which I believe would synthesize on an h1, via browser default bold. That said, I didn’t realize that font-synthesis browser support was so good now wow!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
